+Native legal-roster correction: Rust provenance::legal_assets returns Notice
+assets named airk-cuda-notice-<component>-<leaf>.txt/.html/.md directly under the
+runtime root. windows::observe_package_projection authenticates them and emits
+the same names, sizes and hashes. The projection has no serialized role field.
+Python classifies only these already-authenticated projection rows, enforces a
+safe lowercase direct leaf/prefix/extension and keeps every byte/name unchanged.
+Rust alone validates component membership, original-source identity, Notice role
+and complete legal coverage. Python does not decode a RuntimeManifest or infer
+legal authority from a filename; the native projection and closed original census
+remain mandatory. Nested notices/cuda-runtime names, bare cuda-license.txt,
+renamed/omitted/extra rows and case collisions are refused. Builder, signing and
+installer consumers forward that exact roster; notices remain beside the service
+image. Private provider-only staging remains incomplete and unapproved.
